--- Returns an arrow that ignores its input and always yields `c`.
---
--- @details
--- `constantly` lifts a plain value into arrow position, which is
--- useful wherever the comb API expects a function but the result
--- should not depend on the input -- e.g. a default branch for
--- `comb.choice`, or a constant member of `comb.fanout`.
---
--- @example
--- `f :: 0 >>> comb.constantly`
--- `999 >>> f`
--- -- => 0
---
export constantly :: c ~> _ ~> c
